WEBVTT

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:10.110
I was held captive by the Friday 
Fellows until just a bit ago.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:17.410
It was all the plot of Ebisugawa 
Soun, sitting over there.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.590
A tanuki who boils tanuki in a hot pot?

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.800
We're not talking about tengu or humans here.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.580
Such a cruel tanuki does 
not exist in this world.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.450
This is the truth!

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.650
He's a member of the Shimogamo family, too!

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.300
It appears some people have 
entered the room next door.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.060
1,200 years since Emperor Kammu settled 
on a location for the palace…

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.510
Humans live in the city, 
tanuki crawl the earth,

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:49.810
tengu fly through the air.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.060
Since the Heian era relocation, humans, 
tanuki, and tengu have maintained a delicate balance.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.470
That's what keeps the great wheel of 
this city turning round and round.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:04.490
More fun than anything is 
watching that wheel spin.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:08.120
I'm what you'd call a tanuki,

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.290
but too proud to be a <i>mere</i> tanuki,

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:16.110
I admire tengu from afar 
and love imitating humans.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.480
For that reason, my daily 
life is so dizzyingly busy

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:23.970
<b>Sensuiro</b>

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.210
there's no time to be bored.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.980
<b>Episode 13: 
The Eccentric Family</b>

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:33.110
Compared to Chitose-ya this place 
is a little cramped for seven.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.320
Please forgive us.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.690
Hey, is the next room out of the question?

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.990
There are a great many 
people in the next room.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:44.740
For so many people they're awfully 
quiet. It's like there's no one there.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.960
Yes, they are quiet, aren't they?

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:05.270
So, what are you plotting?

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.390
Not telling.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:11.360
I don't mind as long as it's interesting,

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.960
but don't get too rough.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.270
A delivery has arrived.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:29.170
That's quite a beautiful tanuki.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:33.430
Unusually so. How about it, Daikoku?

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:39.590
This is a fine tanuki, 
wouldn't you say, Hotei?

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.500
What's wrong, Hotei?

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:47.890
Stop with these absurd 
fabrications, Yaichiro!

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.440
It's pathetic.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.710
How dare you...

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:55.460
How dare you lie like that, you slimeball!

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:59.060
Is that any way to talk to your Uncle?

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.840
Learn some manners!

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.400
"Uncle?" You boiled my Father in a hot pot!

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.950
He boiled Soichiro?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.000
Hold on, calm down.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.210
This is just more baseless chatter.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.870
No matter how many lies he tells, 
no one will accept his story

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:24.460
so it seems he's dragged his father 
into this out of desperation.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:27.900
But of course, he has no 
proof of that story either.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.440
Who can prove it?

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.630
Kaisei is our witness! Your daughter!

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:36.720
She's just at that age

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.290
where girls often dream up such tragedies.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:45.430
Aren't you embarrassed to have taken 
my spacey daughter's talk as the truth?

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:49.250
Do you really believe I sent 
Soichiro to the hot pot?

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.250
How long are you gonna keep playing dumb?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.610
Well, you guys keep spouting 
the most outrageous nonsense.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:59.220
What tanuki would believe 
such a horrible story?

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:03.760
How about it? Do you think 
I would do such a thing?

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:12.390
Certainly, there are puzzling aspects to how 
Soichiro ended up as the Friday Fellow's hot pot.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.680
It's strange that a tanuki so great

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:18.750
could so easily fall into 
those humans' hands.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:24.930
However, it'd be a different 
story if he were plastered.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.120
Word on the street is,

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.150
the night Soichiro was captured 
by the Friday Fellows

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:34.540
there was a tanuki drinking with 
him to the end, isn't that right?

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.400
I daresay that's the reason

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.800
Soichiro was captured 
by those hateful humans.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.320
But even now,

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.210
the concerned party has not stepped forward.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:51.770
He's clammed up and is 
instead fabricating reasons

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.790
why the leader of tanuki society 
slipped into an iron pot.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.750
I heard a rumor that he's 
ashamed of his base actions

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:02.280
and has been hiding in 
the well of some temple.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:12.490
I won't let you get away with that!

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:19.230
I don't care if you're my uncle or who you are!

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.250
I'm gonna personally flatten you!

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.310
If you think you can bite me, give it a shot!

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:26.130
At that point, any chance you had 
at becoming Nise-emon would be gone!

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:30.730
Sounds like they're getting 
down to business next door!

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:31.850
 Calm down, Yaichiro! Order! Order!

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.780
Is it Field Day in there or what?

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:45.280
Good heavens, a tiger!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.030
B-Benten!

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:54.280
Boy, tonight's a noisy one.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.380
Oh, Ebisugawa!

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:04.360
Why?! Why do you have that tanuki?

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.840
I thought I left her in the storeroom.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:11.300
Well, there are various reasons, 
but we're borrowing her.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.380
Borrowing her and then what?

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.610
Boiling her in a hot pot.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.640
That's not "borrowing"!

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:20.120
I stated plainly that this 
one could not be boiled!

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.020
That's my tanuki!

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.030
What about "your" tanuki?

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:29.830
Boil anyone except her! I won't allow this!

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:32.660
I won't give you any more Electric Brandy!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.460
Then it's a simple matter of taking it.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:38.840
Isn't that right, Benten?

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.770
Quite so.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:45.920
This is why... This is what 
makes humans so nasty!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.300
What's wrong, Hotei?

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:07.530
This is the one!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.490
The one I nursed!

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.450
I won't let you have her!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:17.650
It's because you let the first one get away

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:20.240
that I went to such great pains to get her!

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:25.280
A year-end bash without a tanuki? 
What of the Friday Fellow tradition?

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:27.620
You'll be ousted from the Fellows, Hotei!

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:30.160
Ousted or whatever is fine!

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.690
Getting uppity, huh!

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:35.040
I was wrong.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:38.560
This is defeat, ideological defeat.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.200
But that's fine!

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:46.560
What's with eating tanuki hot pot for 
kicks in these enlightened times, anyways?

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:50.280
To hell with the Friday Fellows! 
To hell with tradition!

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:53.140
You've eaten a ton of 'em, too, you know.

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:57.040
To eat isn't to love? What 
happened to your theory?

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:58.900
To eat is to love.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:02.180
But to not eat what you 
could eat is also love!

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:06.020
Well you're just saying whatever the 
hell now, aren't you? And so boldly!

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:07.630
Sophistry, pure sophistry!

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:10.380
Sophistry, great! I don't 
require your opinion!

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.010
I've decided on a complete about-face!

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:17.640
Do an about-face if you like, 
but the tanuki stays here.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:26.060
Th-The Friday Fellows!

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:38.120
Well this is a scene of unparalleled beauty!

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.870
We can make as many hot pots as we like.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:51.840
Sorry, 'scuse me.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:12.670
Shut it!

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:15.420
Shut up!

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:29.340
Sheesh, what a mess.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.570
Shut <i>up</i>!

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:40.350
Are you hurt?

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:50.070
Professor, please, if you 
could quell your rage!

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.910
<b>Congratulations to the new Nise-emon!</b>

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.690
How long--

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:13.190
How long do you intend to keep me waiting?!

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:16.800
If you don't quit screwing around, 
I'm gonna blow you all away!

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.290
Nyoigatake Yakushibo!

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:24.520
We've caught them in a compromising position!

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:29.010
What are you saying?! This is a 
misunderstanding, a total misunderstanding!

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:31.890
You!

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:35.480
Human scum like you laying a hand 
on Benten is completely inexcusable.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.600
But it's not just you!

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.690
Every last schmuck here is guilty!

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:44.130
Hear me now! Behold this tengu!

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:48.000
You don't get it? I despise the lot of you!

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.430
For I am a tengu!

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:54.090
You all, without exception, 
need to learn your place!

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.930
<b>Minamiza</b>

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.930
<b>Sensuiro</b>

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:26.240
Here he comes!

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:33.750
Professor, how about we call it 
good and show some forgiveness?

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:51.770
The professor still has 
some fight in him, I see.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.480
Yasaburo, do something!

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.930
Can't you see I'm trying?

00:11:57.930 --> 00:12:01.320
Big Brother, he's taking a break.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:04.990
Here's our chance!

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.800
Gonna die, gonna die!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.760
Really now, you're such a hooligan.

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:27.110
Nice work. I'll take it from here.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.740
Master.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:37.730
Benten?

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:41.980
I think everyone understands the 
terror you represent well enough now.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:43.740
How about it?

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:46.240
But...

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.970
I bought Q-tips.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:51.880
I'll clean your ears for you,

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:54.460
with your head in my lap for 
the first time in a while.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:13:00.110
Professor, could you do me a 
favor and forget about all that?

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:04.910
Let's go home.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:18.500
What are you guys doing 
screwing around out here?

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.520
Better skedaddle back to the the forest!

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:27.050
Hairballs who stay out late get eaten!

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.340
By the way, Yajiro,

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:42.460
how long are you planning on 
staying a frog? Isn't it a pain?

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:46.600
Ahh, I haven't quite got the knack back yet.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:49.910
For the time being I'll 
just have to be a frog.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:52.350
Who'll be Nise-emon?

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:56.850
Well, I committed assault in 
front of the elders, so...

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:02.830
But so many of Soun's misdeeds were 
exposed that there's no way it'll be him.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:07.220
I guess aloha-shirt Yasaka will 
continue on as deputy for a while.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:10.270
Oh right, Mother!

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:14.710
Right, right. I told her to go 
to Akegarasu ahead of us, but...

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:16.700
I wonder if she made it okay.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.540
<b>Please charge</b>

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.950
It's out of battery, though.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.850
No problem!

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:34.640
I just got to Akegarasu.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.590
You're all okay, right?

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:41.890
Yup, we're all here. I'll 
give you to Yasaburo.

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:46.980
Mother, I'm alive 'n kickin'.

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:50.210
Yasaburo? You did a great job.

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:54.850
Oh, it was nothing. Well, here's Yaichiro.

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:59.830
Mother, today was a complete mess.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.550
There are no words to express my apology.

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:07.410
On top of that, I'm sorry to say so,
 but I doubt I'll become Nise-emon.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:12.660
That fine. As long as you're around, 
you'll get another chance.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.060
I'm sorry.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.600
I'll give you to Yajiro.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:34.960
Yajiro? Why aren't you saying anything?

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:37.640
Did you get hurt?

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:46.840
It's been a while, Mother.

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:50.010
I'm sorry I didn't get in touch for so long.

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:53.540
Please forgive me somehow.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.660
It's okay.

00:15:57.530 --> 00:16:01.110
I understand how you feel.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:04.150
So no more crying, okay?

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:10.390
Well, it's certainly been a night.

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:14.430
We're all waiting for you to get here!

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:19.590
Shall we kick things off 
together with a belly strike?

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:23.700
If we do that it'll upset our stomachs.

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:25.560
Yasaburo.

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:26.670
Big Brother!

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:30.980
Well then!

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:44.550
This is some crowd, huh.

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:47.480
Don't want to get crushed, do we?

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:52.490
It's most dangerous for me, 
because anyhow, I'm a frog.

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:57.200
Please don't drop me, 
Yasaburo. I'll get trampled.

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:02.850
Oh, hey you. Happy New Year.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:06.420
Hello and happy New Year to you as well.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.940
May I inquire after your health?

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:11.770
Doing just fine.

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:16.760
But you know, all that stuff, no matter 
how many times I go over it in my head,

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:20.600
I have no idea what happened that night.

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:25.990
Went through hell, though. Got 
booted from the Friday Fellows.

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:29.730
But, if you're doing well 
now, isn't that good enough?

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:33.100
Well, yeah, in the end, you're right.

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.860
Come see me in my office again sometime!

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:44.560
Hey, take a look at that.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.350
Kurama tengu?

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:56.670
There's no telling how many of these 
people are actually tengu and tanuki.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:18:00.980
Well, in this day and age, even a frog 
can visit a shrine for New Year's.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:04.220
Tengu make New Year's wishes, too, huh.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:07.390
And what's wrong with a tengu 
making a New Year's wish?

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:13.120
Well if it isn't Nyoigatake Yakushibo!

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:15.550
Happy New Year!

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:17.010
Indeed.

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:18.920
Are you on your way to the shrine?

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:23.410
That was our intention, 
but it's become a chore.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:26.660
Oh come now, let's visit the shrine.

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:29.870
Right, Professor? It's only once a year.

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:33.870
I guess you're right. Dealing with a crowd 
now and then isn't the end of the world.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:36.760
Yaichiro.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.190
Yes?

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:41.890
You should go with the flow a bit more.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.820
Uh-- understood.

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:45.140
Yajiro.

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:49.560
For starters, you should quit being a frog.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.730
Okay.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:52.150
Yashiro.

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:56.050
For the time being, you 
should hurry up and grow!

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.030
Got it!

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:09.920
Well, there's nothing for us 
to do standing around here.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.430
Shall we go?

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:23.370
Hey there, Kinkaku, Ginkaku. Happy New Year.

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:25.350
Getting a head-start on your idiocy this year, I see.

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:28.730
You got us good that night, huh, Yasaburo.

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:33.090
We caught a horrible cold and spent 
the whole time until today in bed!

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.800
I thought I was gonna die.

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:39.790
They say the stupid ones don't catch 
colds, but I guess idiots do, huh.

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:41.020
What was that?!

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:42.320
Hey!

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:49.080
Can my idiot brothers not even 
give a proper New Year's greeting?

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.040
"Idiot"?

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.820
You too?

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:53.670
Kaisei?

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.850
It's fine, just go.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:58.800
Hmph!

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:01.050
Kaisei!

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:08.760
I've never seen her, so I wouldn't 
know who to look for anyhow...

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:16.040
Did Uncle come back?

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:18.750
No, he said he was going to 
a hot spring and that was it.

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:21.030
He might never come back.

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:24.910
How about if you quit messing 
around and let me see you?

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:27.730
You'll never find me!

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:42.680
I have a ton of things to wish for.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:45.550
Because you're so greedy.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:47.600
Am I really that greedy?

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:52.510
If you don't narrow down your goal, even 
a wish that might have come true won't.

00:20:52.510 --> 00:20:54.070
Hmm, in that case...

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:58.290
I'll wish to meet the one I'm destined for.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:01.610
There you go acting like a cutie 
again, saying stuff like that.

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:05.360
So what are you gonna wish for, Yasaburo?

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:10.910
Huh. I thought about it,

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:14.710
but I don't have any wishes in particular.

00:21:14.970 --> 00:21:20.130
As long as we're all living, as long as 
we're all having fun, that should do it, right?

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:22.630
We're tanuki.

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:27.800
If someone were to ask me how tanuki should 
live their lives, this is how I would answer.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:33.220
The tanuki wriggling about in Kyoto 
should abandon all lofty ambitions.

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:37.650
There's nothing else we have to do 
besides lead an interesting life.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.200
Yasaburo?

00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:45.610
There's nothing I need to ask for.

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:58.120
Just some moderate glory for 
my family and our friends.

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:35.350
<b>We truly thank you for watching!</b>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:39.920
<b>Deep gratitude!</b>
